        "by": "human",
        "reason": "Downstream SQL-on-FHIR consumers join derived tables on getResourceKey() resource keys, which the port computes internally but drops at the outermost SELECT. The attempt adds the paired key column beside each MIMIC identifier column (subject_id->patient_key, hadm_id->encounter_key, stay_id->icu_encounter_key, specimen_id->specimen_key). Additive and shape-only: both comparison paths project manifest columns explicitly, so no compared value can change. The MIMIC integer columns are retained as the oracle join keys.",
        "superseded_decided_by": "judge",
        "superseded_error": null,
        "superseded_justification": "Coagulation attempt_0004 is a contested review with 115 differing_conflict rows, all confined to charttime, and zero only_oracle, only_candidate, or differing_null_only rows. Upstream mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_observation_labevents.sql:15 casts relational lab.charttime through TIMESTAMPTZ, and line 121 writes that transformed value to Observation.effectiveDateTime. For nonexistent spring-forward 02:xx wall times, this normalizes to 03:xx; genuine 03:xx values serialize identically, making the operation many-to-one with no FHIR marker from which any query could recover the original 02:xx. mimic-fhir/sql/fhir_specimen_lab.sql:9,18,58 independently aggregates charttime, repeats the destructive TIMESTAMPTZ cast, and writes it to Specimen.collection.collectedDateTime, so that path cannot recover the filtered source value either. Attempt_0004 applies direct TIMESTAMP_NTZ parsing and final TIMESTAMP_NTZ output; all defensible mappings were exhausted. The result reproduces 1,542,888/1,543,003 rows identically: 99.9925% overall and representable fidelity, with 115/1,543,003 affected (about 0.0075%). Coagulation has no divergent dependencies.",
        "superseded_status": "COMPLETED_WITH_DIVERGENCE"
      },
